What:		/sys/class/drm/card*/device/agx_stats
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Asahi Linux GPU driver maintainers
Description:
		Legacy GPU format. For T8140 G17P, see sysfs-driver-asahi
		for the version 2 format and power-state validity rules.

		Read-only dump of the AGX firmware statistics decoded by the
		drm/asahi driver. The driver already polls the firmware statistics
		ring (see `drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/channel.rs::StatsChannel::poll`,
		`drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/fw/channels.rs::StatsMsg`) and exposes the
		latest values via this file.

		The file is owned by the platform device
		`/sys/devices/platform/<...>.gpu/`, which is symlinked from the
		`device` entry of the matching DRM card under `/sys/class/drm/`.

		One `key value` pair per line. Lines are ASCII integer values
		unless noted. Unknown keys may be appended in future firmware
		versions and must be ignored by readers.

		Module parameter `asahi.stats_export` (default 1) controls
		whether the driver retains the values. When 0, the file shows
		`unsupported` (the firmware messages are still polled but
		discarded).

		Access: Read-only. Owner-readable (mode 0444).

		busy_ns    cumulative u64; utilization-weighted busy time in
		           nanoseconds since boot: each Utilization message window
		           contributes its duration scaled by the busiest subqueue
		           percentage. Firmware timestamps are base-clock ticks
		           (HwConfig.base_clock_hz, 24 MHz on every supported SoC)
		           and are converted to ns by the driver. Monotonic;
		           bounded by elapsed wall time. MEASURED on T6021
		           (M2 Max, 13.5): idle desktop fraction ~0.01, saturated
		           4096^2 fp16 matmul fraction ~1.0 (util1..4 = 100).
		           T6001 shares the message format and the 24 MHz clock
		           (fw 13.5); the same idle-vs-matmul check must be run
		           there before the magnitude claim is repeated.

		jobs       u64; cumulative completed submissions since boot.
		           Counted on the host at submission completion (when
		           the last command of a submission completes and its
		           fence signals), not from a firmware counter.

		pstate     u32; current performance state index (PowerState.pstate).

		power_mw   u32; latest average power reading in milliwatts
		           (AvgPower.avg_power). May be 0 if the firmware has not
		           yet reported AvgPower.

		util1..util4   u32; raw `Utilization` fields from the firmware,
		           unscaled. Semantics (firmware tick vs % vs MHz) are
		           validated against a controlled MLX load and may
		           differ per SoC revision. Treat as raw until a per-chip
		           doc note lands.

		temperature_raw, temperature_scale    u32; latest Temperature
		           sample and scale (or 0 if Temperature has not yet
		           arrived).

		Field meanings (units, window, saturation) are documented in
		`drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/stats.rs` and may evolve with firmware
		revisions. busy_ns is monotonic non-decreasing while the device
		is bound (it only accumulates). The snapshot struct is
		`#[repr(C)]` on the Rust side and its offsets are asserted at
		build time in `sysfs.c`; readers must parse `key value` lines and
		must not assume binary layout of this file.
		G17 firmware has no supported decoder for this snapshot format;
		its file reports unsupported rather than fabricated zero counters.
